        "original_id": "63f357c5-d646-5347-99cd-1561dcd0f1c3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Pablo Trapero, Aleksander Ford, Mieczysława Ćwiklińska, Jerzy Leszczyński, Władysław Godik\n- Films: Crane World, Border Street\n- Places: Argentina, Kiev, Naples, Florida, United States, Soviet Union\n- Roles: film producer, editor, director, head of the Polish People's Army Film Crew\n- Topics: World War II, Polish cinema, Argentine cinema\n\nFacts:\n- Aleksander Ford was born as Mosze Lifszyc on 24 November 1908 in Kiev, Russian Empire.\n- Pablo Trapero was born on 4 October 1971.\n- During World War II, Aleksander Ford served as head of the Polish People's Army Film Crew in the Soviet Union.\n- Border Street, also titled Ulica Graniczna, is a 1948 Polish drama film directed by Aleksander Ford and starring Mieczysława Ćwiklińska, Jerzy Leszczyński, and Władysław Godik.\n- Crane World, also titled Mundo grúa, is a 1999 Argentine film written and directed by Pablo Trapero.\n- Pablo Trapero is an Argentine film producer, editor, and director.\n- Aleksander Ford was a Polish Jewish film director.\n- Aleksander Ford died on 4 April 1980 in Naples, Florida, United States.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
